# Search inputs

Never show the browser’s default search clear control (the blue circled **x**). Search fields are a simple blank underline.

- Use `type="text"` with the `.search` class. Do not use `type="search"` — Chrome/Safari draw a clear button on it.
- Do not add a custom clear icon unless the user asks for one.
- The cancel-button reset in `app/assets/css/main.css` is a fallback only. Do not rely on it and reintroduce `type="search"`.

```html
<!-- BAD: browser draws a blue x once the field has text -->
<input type="search" placeholder="Search locations…">

<!-- GOOD -->
<input class="search" type="text" placeholder="Search locations…">
```
